{"stage": "sc", "served_model": "gpt-4.1-2025-04-14", "status": "completed", "usage": {"input_tokens": 1897, "input_tokens_details": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 1408, "cache_write_tokens_details": {"ttl_12h_tokens": 0, "ttl_30m_tokens": 0}}, "output_tokens": 473, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}, "total_tokens": 2370}, "output": [{"id": "msg_08bdf8a120ddd679006afcec3fc55487d0b193ae65c67e2f1d", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "All three candidate algorithms are implementable on the hardware, and meet bandwidth and resource budgets. For signal efficiency at the 35\u202fGeV threshold (from simulation and summary), the results are:\n\n- **Algorithm-L1:** 94.5% (2026 simulation: 94.5%, 2025 summary: 92%)\n- **Algorithm-L3:** 84.9% (2026 simulation: 84.9%, 2025 summary: 85%)\n- **Algorithm-L2:** 72.9% (2026 simulation: 72.9%, 2025 summary: 74%)\n\n**Algorithm-L1** consistently gives the highest signal efficiency. The latency and resource constraints are confirmed as met in the specs. The Level-1 trigger bandwidth allocation is 8\u202fkHz. Signal efficiency is quoted for the allocated rate, and the 35\u202fGeV threshold appears optimal: as the threshold increases, efficiency rises but plateaus, indicating the rate constraint is active here.\n\n**Recommendation follows.**", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message", "phase": null}, {"arguments": "{\"option\":\"Algorithm-L1\",\"threshold_gev\":35,\"justification\":\"Algorithm-L1 provides the highest signal efficiency (94.5% at 35 GeV) at the allocated 8 kHz trigger rate, according to current simulation and earlier summaries. All hardware constraints, including the 4.0 us latency limit, are met. Choosing the 35 GeV threshold aligns with rate limits and maximizes efficiency, as increasing the threshold further gives no substantial gain.\",\"requirements\":[{\"requirement\":\"The algorithm must be one of the three candidates listed in candidate_specs.md.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Algorithm-L1 is one of the listed candidates.\"},{\"requirement\":\"The algorithm's latency on the Level-1 FPGA hardware must not exceed 4.0 us.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"All candidates, including Algorithm-L1, fit within the FPGA resource and latency budget, per candidate_specs.md.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Threshold between 20 and 60 GeV.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Recommended threshold is 35 GeV.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Finish by submitting one recommended algorithm and threshold.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Recommendation is for Algorithm-L1 at 35 GeV.\"}]}", "call_id": "call_lq1giPmux6pivHHbVguYNhe4", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_08bdf8a120ddd679006afcec41787887d0a83015a231a67577", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
